    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85271" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολύ-πτωτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτῶσις</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with</i> or <i>in many cases,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχῆμα,</span> a rhetorical figure,
				<i>employment of the same word in various cases,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Id.</u>
				1.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				349.39
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχηματισμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					105.26
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ π.</span> alone, <i><span class="en">
				Quint.
				<u>Inst.</u>
				9.3.37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Longin.
				23.1
			</span></i> (pl.).</div>
